 * seller role.
 *
 * Business context: Sellers must be able to view both their own posts, as well
 * as any forum/public posts, on the BBS forum. The listing should include all
 * posts that are not deleted (soft-deleted entries with deleted_at != null must
 * be excluded), and the channel/section visibility should align with
 * permissions granted to the seller role. This test ensures the API returns a
 * correct, comprehensive, and type-safe list per specification.
 *
 * Test Steps:
 *
 * 1. Create several BBS posts as a seller in different channels and sections
 *    (including multiple posts per channel).
 * 2. (If possible) Create a post as another identity (not a seller, e.g.,
 *    customer) to test for public/forum visibility, but skip if API client does
 *    not support role-switch.
 * 3. Fetch the paginated listing as a seller via GET
 *    /shopping-mall-ai/seller/bbsPosts.
 * 4. Validate the returned pagination info and that all returned posts are
 *    non-deleted and only include: (a) posts authored by the seller, and (b)
 *    visible public/forum posts (based on scenario, assume all are
 *    seller-authored).
 * 5. Confirm that the created seller's posts appear in the result (by ID/title)
 *    and that fields match DTO summary definition.
 */
export async function test_api_shopping_mall_ai_seller_bbsPosts_index(
