 * - The API should return not found (404) or forbidden (403), and must NOT return
 *   private data under any circumstances.
 *
 * The workflow is as follows:
 *
 * 1. As an admin, create a coupon with restricted access such that it is not
 *    assigned to (or available to) the current test customer. This can be
 *    achieved by scoping the coupon to an unrelated seller, or by internal test
 *    logic.
 * 2. As a regular customer, attempt to fetch this coupon by its ID using the GET
 *    /shopping-mall-ai/customer/coupons/{couponId} endpoint.
 * 3. Validate that the API responds with an error:
 *
 *    - The error must be either a 404 Not Found, 403 Forbidden, or analogous (do not
 *         care about error message specifics).
 *    - The API must not return the coupon details or expose any data about the
 *         private coupon.
 *
 * Edge cases:
 *
 * - Customer is not among the coupon recipients and should be blocked.
 * - Coupon is not globally available but has valid active status.
 * - No leakage of private coupon fields or identifiers when blocked.
 */
export async function test_api_shopping_mall_ai_customer_coupons_test_get_coupon_details_for_private_coupon_not_assigned_to_customer(
